If you're doing this for a Mac, there are some things to be aware of.
The Mac needs to partition it's code so that no short jump exceeds 32k.
Even data segments have to be under 32k big.  Even the old list of monsters
had to be divided.  The new one may have to be divided a number of times.  

Also, note that in text files, Macs usually don't take a linefeed as well
as a carriage return.  They only need the carriage return symbol.  So instead
of doing a binary transfer of text files from ftp host to mac, be sure to
do a text transfer of text files from ftp host to mac, that will automatically
do the conversion for you.

